# Normalize line endings to LF on checkout, on every platform. Without this, a
# Windows CI runner's git checkout can silently convert committed LF endings to
# CRLF depending on that runner's core.autocrlf setting -- which is exactly what
# caused a Windows-only Checkstyle false divergence on an otherwise-passing PR:
# an empty `//` paragraph-break comment line becomes a comment containing a
# stray trailing \r once checked out as CRLF, and Checkstyle's
# singleLineCommentStartWithSpace check treats that differently than a
# genuinely empty comment, failing only on windows-latest while
# macos-latest/ubuntu-latest (LF checkouts) passed the identical source.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts conventionally require CRLF to run correctly.
*.bat text eol=crlf
